{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "John Meets Sandra", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "How Did It Go?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 7, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn5le07ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Agreeing and Disagreeing", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use different phrases to agree and disagree tactfully (politely).<br/> Generally, you use the Simple Present Tense in the affirmative to agree. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Don't you think coconut water is good for your body?</br><span class=\"strong\">Sandra</span>: Absolutely.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Sandra</span>: Coffee isn't healthy for you.</br> <span class=\"strong\">John</span>: That's not always true.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "At the workplace, we ask for others' opinion with questions such as:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul> <li>What do you think?</li> <li>I'm interested in your feedback/input.</li> <li>Please let me know your thoughts.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We show agreement or disagreement with statements in the chart below.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Agreeing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Disagreeing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I agree with you 100 percent.</br> I couldn't agree with you more.</br> That's so true.</br> You're absolutely right.</br> Absolutely.</br> That's exactly how I feel.</br> Exactly.</br> You have a point there.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I don't think so.</br> I'm afraid I disagree.</br> I beg to differ.</br> Not necessarily.</br> That's not always true.</br> I'm not sure if ...</br> I see what you're saying, but ...</br> I don't know about that ...\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Comparatives & Superlatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use adjectives to compare two things. These are called <span class=\"strong\">comparative</span> adjectives. You can also use adjectives to compare one item with the rest of a group. These are called <span class=\"strong\">superlative</span> adjectives.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Selling good quality products is <span class=\"underline\">as</span> important <span class=\"underline\">as</span> good customer service.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There are <span class=\"underline\">more</span> people at this workshop <span class=\"underline\">than</span> the last one.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There was <span class=\"underline\">less</span> time allotted for the last workshop <span class=\"underline\">than</span> this one.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "For comparative adjectives, you can use the structure:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">as</span> + adjective + <span class=\"strong\">as</span> </br>adjective (<span class=\"strong\">-er</span>) <span class=\"strong\">than</span></br> <span class=\"strong\">more/less</span> + adjective + <span class=\"strong\">than</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Adjectives with 3 syllables or more use <span class=\"strong italic\">more/less</span> + <span class=\"italic\">adjective</span> + <span class=\"strong italic\">than</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For superlative adjectives, you can use:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul> <li>adjective  (<span class=\"strong\">-est</span>)</li> <li><span class=\"strong\">most/least</span> + adjective</li> </ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Adjectives with 3 syllables or more use <span class=\"strong italic\">most/least</span> + <span class=\"italic\">adjective</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The adjectives <span class=\"italic\">good</span> and <span class=\"italic\">bad</span> are irregular adjectives. They do not follow the same rules.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Good ----> better-----> best</br> Bad -----> worse -----> worst", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to participate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to join in an activity or event", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's important that all employees participate in this workshop.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le07ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about work.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to register", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put your name in to join an activity or event", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You must register for the workshop before attending.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le07ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "let me know your thoughts", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to ask someone about their ideas or thoughts", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let me know your thoughts on the new system at work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le07ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to demonstrate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to show with action how to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sandra demonstrated how to do a good presentation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le07ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "electronic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used with a computer or the Internet", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: An electronic reservation system would be easier and faster than a paper system.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le07ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to establish", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put a system or relationship firmly in place", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sandra established a good relationship with her clients.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le07ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "rapport", "type": "name"}, {"content": "good friendly relations with others", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's a good idea to have a good rapport with all your customers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le07ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Write 3 sentences on how you bought movie tickets or train tickets 10 years ago. Use past tense verbs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 3 sentences comparing this old system to how you buy these tickets now.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell your partner your opinion and ask for their opinion on the two systems.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write complete statements on things I did in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make comparisons between old and new procedures.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I tell others my opinion and ask others for their opinion.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn5le07ob09re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn5le07ob09re2img05.jpg", "time": "10", "id": 1, "text": "John receives an e-mail from his boss, Mr. Micklewhite:</br><br/>\n<span class=\"italic\">micklewhite@cruisemail.com wrote:</span></br>\nHello, John. I understand you participated in the workshop on customer service last week. There were more people than in other past workshops. I'm interested in your feedback on it. I think more tour guides should register. Please let me know your thoughts.</p>"}, {"image": "engenn5le07ob09re2img06.jpg", "time": "18000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"italic\">John.Harris@mail.com wrote:</span></br>\nHello, Mr. Micklewhite. The workshop was really helpful for me. I certainly agree more guides would find it useful. However, I'm not sure if every guide will have time to attend. Sandra did a fantastic job. I learned about more efficient reservation procedures."}, {"image": "engenn5le07ob09re2img08.jpg", "time": "35000", "id": 3, "text": "Sandra demonstrated how an electronic system is faster than a paper and pen system. She also established a good rapport with the group. It was the best workshop ever on this ship. I hope future workshops will be as interesting as this was."}], "audiosrc": "engenn5le07ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le07ob09re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can agree and disagree tactfully.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk or report about actions, events or people. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can make comparisons.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Tell your friend about your favorite movie. Ask them what they think.", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Do you agree or disagree with them?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Compare your favorite movie with your partner's.", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}],